# Generated by appkit firebase-merge (npm run firebase -- generate).
#
# 🛑 These four are NOT ignored, deliberately. They were listed here AND tracked
# at the same time, which does nothing — .gitignore has no effect on an
# already-tracked path — while conditioning everyone to treat them as noise in
# `git status`. That is the recipe for committing a stale copy or reverting a
# fresh one.
#
# They must stay TRACKED: `firebase.json` deploys the root copies, so a deploy
# is only reproducible from the commit if they are in it. Drift against
# `appkit/firebase/base/` is prevented by `scripts/audit-firebase-rules-generated.mjs`,
# which regenerates and diffs on every `npm run check`.
#
# Project-specific rules go in `appkit.config.js` -> `firebase.{database,firestore,storage}`,
# never by hand-editing the generated file — the next generate overwrites it.

