# Tester plugin run artifacts — live production session cookies, screenshots and
# the preserve-tier backup (which contains the encrypted siteSettings credentials).
/tester/.tester-runs/
/claude-tester-report.md
# NOTE: docs/TEST-RUN-DEFECTS.md is deliberately NOT ignored. It is the durable
# consolidated defect register and MUST be committed — the whole lesson of the
# cleanup that produced it is that an untracked finding is one `rm` from gone,
# and .tester-runs/ is ignored in this repo AND in the tester submodule.
# Regenerate with `node scripts/test-run-defects.mjs`.

# Stray verdict scratch file from ad-hoc tester diagnostics
/x.json

# Generated on demand by tester/scripts/make-media-fixtures.mjs --with-oversized:
# >10MB of incompressible noise whose only job is to trip the image size cap.
# Reproducible in a second; not worth carrying in git.
public/test-media/oversized.png
docs/*TESTING-*
docs/TRIAGE-*

# Tester screenshots land at the repo root from the Playwright MCP.
# They are evidence for a run, not source — never commit them.
/*.png

# Downloaded taxonomy cover images — a STAGING CACHE, not source.
#
# `scripts/fetch-taxonomy-images.mjs` fills this from beyblade.fandom.com and
# `scripts/upload-taxonomy-images.mjs` pushes it to Firebase Storage, after
# which the seed references `/media/<shortId>` and nothing reads these files
# again. Committing ~195 binaries (4.3 MB) to carry bytes that already live in
# Storage would bloat every clone and every Vercel upload for no reader.
#
# Reproducible without them: both scripts are committed and idempotent, and
# `docs/research/bey-corpus-2026-10/image-provenance.json` records the exact
# source URL of every file.
/.media-cache/

# Statutory business documents — GST certificate, Udyam registration, bank
# passbook. These live under public/ for convenience while being prepared for
# upload, and public/ is served VERBATIM by Next.js: no rewrite intercepts
# /business, so an unignored file here is reachable at
# https://www.letitrip.in/business/<name> the moment it deploys. The Vercel CLI
# respects .gitignore when uploading (the same mechanism that keeps appkit/dist
# out), and .vercelignore repeats these rules belt-and-braces.
#
# 🛑 A PATTERN, not three exact filenames. The previous rules were pinned to
# literal names, so a re-issued certificate or a re-downloaded
# passbook_<newtimestamp>.pdf would have silently failed to match — and the
# passbook line pointed at a file that had already been deleted.
#
# The QR is the deliberate exception: a UPI collect QR exists to be scanned by
# buyers, so it is tracked and public. It must also stay a STATIC asset rather
# than being served through /api/media/[...slug], which watermarks every image
# it serves with no opt-out and would corrupt the code.
public/business/*
!public/business/payment-qr.jpg
authentic data/*
.tmplog/*
docs/*

# Ad-hoc diagnostic scripts — never part of the build.
tmp-*.mjs
.tmp*/
